<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs end firmer in NY as Dow loses 21 points.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs end firmer in NY as Dow loses 21 points.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs ended firmer in New York on Tuesday, where the Dow Industrials lost 20.71 points to 5,874.03.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia.</p>
<p>Company    Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>Tranz Rail     N.Y.    US$14 7/8	   nil</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$22 3/8	 +0 1/8</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$24	     +0 1/8</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$19 7/8	 +0 1/8</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$14 5/8	 +0 1/4</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$77 1/4	 +0 5/8</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  34 1/2	    -0 1/2</p>
<p>Brierley	 London  64		    nil</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  227 1/2	   -0 1/2</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col  London  155 1/2	   +0 1/2</p>
<p>Templeton	London  134 1/2	   -0 1/4</p>
<p>Lion	     Sydney  A$3.30		nil</p>
<p>Goodman	  Sydney  A$1.29		nil</p>
<p>Macraes	  Sydney  A$3.24		nil</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
